                        "entry_id": "7bbbf043-dc74-352a-96eb-426a23f17f13",
                        "glosses": [
                            "As much as is taken up between the thumb and two first fingers; a pinch."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "also",
                            "figuratively",
                            "obsolete"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "2722e050-d7d1-4411-bc48-f99bf0fc5521",
                                "sense_id": "ef913f69-f977-3574-99de-3b2b8988da17",
                                "text": "Take violets , and infuse a good pugil of them in a quart of vinegar"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "98e8ce89-3d96-46a4-a1ba-282a1c26a644",
                                "sense_id": "ef913f69-f977-3574-99de-3b2b8988da17",
                                "text": "Cinnamon, an ounce and a half; Rosemary flowers, six pugils […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3f676bce-b039-447c-8a63-2cb084d09d21",
                                "sense_id": "ef913f69-f977-3574-99de-3b2b8988da17",
                                "text": "Note, That by Parts is to be understood a Pugil; which is no more than one does usually take up between the Thumb and the two next Fingers."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "1c81b25f-9aa2-437d-a5e9-bcc2b5e63bcf",
                                "sense_id": "ef913f69-f977-3574-99de-3b2b8988da17",
                                "text": "This kind of success was all luck, and if a man had only a given amount for his own share, it was a shame to fritter away so much as a pugil."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
